     "result_text_tail": "s drafted, without a review stop.\n- **The $40M ambition:** read as $40M of US revenue in 2030.\n- **Excluded figures:** the trade-press $5.2B was left out because it also counts makeup and hair care; a footnote says so.\n- **Japan:** the pack gives no working capital for Japan, so its cash figures exclude it (footnoted).\n- **Model conventions:** all of these are stated on the slides.\n  - Stores are open for the full year.\n  - Set-up costs and fixtures count as costs when they are paid.\n  - Inventory is four months of product, freight and duty cost.\n\n**QA**\n- `check.py`: 0 fails and 1 warning. The pack writes \"four months\" in words, so the checker can't match the number; the quote is correct.\n- `render.py`: no layout warnings.\n- `verify.py` wasn't needed, since there are no web sources.\n\n**Not visually checked:** the sandbox blocks PowerPoint, Keynote and Quick Look, so I checked the deck by reading back its text and chart values, not by viewing it. Please look through the slides once in PowerPoint.\n\n**Changed because of renderer limits:** the dashed line for a limit only works on charts that start at zero, and the waterfall chart draws wrongly when its running total goes below zero. So on the cumulative-cash slide, the $18M cap appears as a share in the sidebar rather than as a line. The Amazon-led-versus-retail-led comparison is a bar chart of plus and minus amounts rather than a waterfall.\n\nNext, I can switch to another theme or add a slide that tests different volume levels."
